@bank all
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 2 (FX17's word list): the Sunday swap meet (tradition id market), 10:30-12:30 on the promenade
// stalls; host Orla Ishikawa (the crew store; she keeps a list, of course). Keys, as FX17 named them:
//   swap.open        Orla opens the meet (card or bubble, 90 or fewer).
//   swap.thing.1-3   a stallholder (any goer) shows you a thing; three slots, three things each, so 9 rotate.
//   swap.reply.1-3   your three buttons; swap.after.N is the stallholder's answer to swap.reply.N.
//   swap.stall       stallholders' bubbles (60 or fewer); swap.browse: browsers' bubbles (60 or fewer).
//   swap.close       optional: Orla closes the meet.
// Things already canon at the swap meet: Kovac swapped a scarf for buttons; Holt buys mints; Cruz brings Gerald cuttings;
// Pell's rusted music box came from it; everyone haggles with the Captain. Nobody here sells for credits: things swap.

== swap.open
- Good morning, everyone. Stalls are open. One thing for one thing, and be kind about it.
- Hello, hello. The swap meet's open. Swap fair. I'm keeping a list. Of course I am.   #funny
- Morning. Lay your things out nicely. If it isn't yours to swap, it goes back. Enjoy.

== swap.thing.1
- This paperback's only slightly bent. The ending's good. I won't tell you it.
- A chess set. One knight's a button now. He plays just as well.   #funny
- A puzzle of the Wren. A thousand pieces. Well. Nine hundred and ninety-eight.   #funny
== swap.thing.2
- A knitted tea cosy. It's a bit lopsided. So is the teapot, so it fits.   #funny
- Two pairs of thick socks. Clean, I promise. Too warm for me. Perfect for you.
- A hand-drawn star map. The stars are right. The labels are mostly right.
== swap.thing.3
- A wind-up torch. Wind it for a minute, it shines for two. Bargain, really.
- A jar of odd buttons. Nobody knows where they came from. That's the charm.
- A pressed-flower bookmark from the garden. Cruz didn't see. Cruz never sees.   #funny

// Your three buttons, then the stallholder's answer to each (swap.after.N answers swap.reply.N).
== swap.reply.1
- I'll swap you something for it.
== swap.after.1
- Deal. Shake on it. Pleasure doing business.
- Done. Look after it. It's had a good life so far.   #warm
== swap.reply.2
- What's the story behind it?
== swap.after.2
- It's been on three ships before this one. It always finds a new home on a Sunday.
- Came from a stall on Hesper Dock, years back. Its turn to travel again.
== swap.reply.3
- Just looking, thanks.
== swap.after.3
- Course. Have a wander. It'll be here if you change your mind.
- No rush. Half the fun's the looking.

== swap.stall
- Everything must go. Well. Some things.   #funny
- One thing for one thing. That's the rule.
- Have a look. No pressure. Lots of socks.   #funny
- Fair swaps only. Orla's got the list.
- Mind that jar. It's full of buttons.
- Swapping a puzzle. Most of the pieces are in.   #funny

== swap.browse
- Ooh, what's that one?
- Is that a whole chess set? Nearly whole?
- I've got nothing to swap. I'm just nosy.   #funny
- Came for a scarf. Leaving with a puzzle.   #funny
- Someone's swapping Gerald cuttings. Of course they are.
- Who knitted the tea cosy? It's lovely.
- I'll give you a biscuit for that. Two biscuits.
- Last week's paperback is back. Somebody didn't like it.   #funny

== swap.close
- That's the swap meet. Take your things home, and thank you. The list balances.   #warm
- Half past twelve, everyone. Lovely swapping. Same time next Sunday.
